SUMMARY:Serbia: Minimum wage set at RSD 405 an hour for 2027
DESCRIPTION:Upcoming\, 1 Jan 2027. The Government adopted a decision settin
 g the minimum price of labour for January-December 2027 at RSD 405 per wor
 king hour\, excluding tax and social insurance contributions\, an increase
  of 9.2 percent. The monthly minimum wage will be RSD 70\,470.\n\nSource: 
 https://www.srbija.gov.rs/vest/994489/vlada-usvojila-predlog-zakona-o-reba
 lansu-budzeta-za-2026-godinu.php\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.
 eu/countries/serbia.html#rs-minimum-wage-2027\n\nFor information only\, no
 t legal or tax advice. Sources last checked 1 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/serbia.html#rs-minimum-wage
 -2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:serbia-rs-non-taxable-amount-2027@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261001T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270102
SUMMARY:Serbia: Non-taxable part of salary rises to RSD 37\,369 from 2027
DESCRIPTION:Upcoming\, 1 Jan 2027. The Law amending the Personal Income Tax
  Law (Official Gazette 80/2026\, in force from 8 September 2026) sets the 
 monthly reduction of the salary tax base for a full-time employee at RSD 3
 7\,369. The amending law applies from 1 January 2027. Salary tax stays at 
 10 percent.\n\nSource: https://www.mfin.gov.rs/upload/media/MOq4eO_6aa14ac
 8c7a47.docx\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/serbia.h
 tml#rs-non-taxable-amount-2027\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax 
 advice. Sources last checked 1 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/countries/serbia.html#rs-non-taxable-
 amount-2027
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
